A '''spice mine''' on [[Kessel/Legends|Kessel]] was abandoned by the time of the [[Galactic Empire/Legends|Galactic Empire]]. It was the location of the [[Conclave on Kessel]], a gathering of Jedi and an ill-fated attempt to lure the Sith into the open.

==Specifications==
The former mine had been exhausted, so it was accordingly abandoned, along with much of the equipment. According to [[Shadday Potkin/Legends|Shadday Potkin]], not even the [[Spice spider/Legends|spice spiders]] gathered there any more, though she did caution that it wouldn't be wise to linger long.

It was a large, vaguely rectangular cavern with self illuminated panels affixed to the walls. It had one large mining crane and numerous [[Repulsorlift/Legends|repulsorlift]] mining carts, still full of rock and ore. It apparently also had an [[Oxygen/Legends|oxygen]] processor or filter of some sort, as the cavern still contained breathable air.

Much of the derelict equipment appeared relatively intact.

==History==
After the execution of [[Order 66/Legends|Order 66]], the mine was used as the location for a [[Conclave on Kessel|gathering]] of [[Jedi/Legends|Jedi]]. In attendance were [[Shadday Potkin/Legends|Shadday Potkin]], [[Bultar Swan/Legends|Bultar Swan]], [[Tsui Choi/Legends|Tsui Choi]], [[Roblio Darté]], [[Sia-Lan Wezz]], [[Ma'kis'shaalas/Legends|Ma'kis'shaalas]], [[Koffi Arana]], and [[Jastus Farr]].

However, in reality, one of the Jedi present; Shadday Potkin; attempted to turn the Jedi gathering into a trap for the Sith. She leaked false information that [[Obi-Wan Kenobi/Legends|Obi-Wan Kenobi]] would be present at the gathering, attracting the attention of [[Anakin Skywalker/Legends|Darth Vader]].

Just as Potkin predicted, Vader arrived, unheeding and alone.

In the subsequent battle, Vader managed to kill three of the Jedi, both with his [[Lightsaber/Legends|lightsaber]] and with a [[Cortosis sword/Legends|cortosis blade]] he procured from the slain Potkin. Bultar Swan had been killed by one of her fellows to procure her lightsaber. The remaining three Jedi; Tsui Choi, Roblio Darté and Jastus Farr; attacked Vader telekinetically, hurling the contents of the derelict mining carts at Vader, leaving him horribly injured and partially buried.

The remaining Jedi were slain by the sudden appearance of [[Stormtrooper/Legends|stormtroopers]] from Vader's [[501st Legion/Legends|501st Legion]].

